-- title:
--   The Galois group of the n-th cyclotomic extension is (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ
-- statement:
--   **The Galois group of a cyclotomic extension.** Let $n\ge1$, let $K$ be a field and let $L=K(\zeta_n)$ be the $n$-th cyclotomic extension of $K$, generated by a primitive $n$-th root of unity $\zeta_n$. If the cyclotomic polynomial $\Phi_n$ is irreducible over $K$, then
--   $$\operatorname{Gal}(L/K)\cong(\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^\times.$$
--   The isomorphism sends $\sigma$ to the class $a$ with $\sigma(\zeta_n)=\zeta_n^a$.
--
--   Over $\mathbb Q$ the irreducibility of $\Phi_n$ is Gauss's theorem, so $\operatorname{Gal}(\mathbb Q(\zeta_n)/\mathbb Q)\cong(\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^\times$. This is the starting point of class field theory over $\mathbb Q$: the Kronecker–Weber theorem says that every abelian extension of $\mathbb Q$ lies in some $\mathbb Q(\zeta_n)$. It also gives the constructible regular polygons.
--
--   **Formalization note.** Mathlib's `IsCyclotomicExtension.autEquivPow`. `IsCyclotomicExtension {n} K L` says that $L$ is generated over $K$ by primitive $n$-th roots of unity and contains one. The statement asserts that there is a group isomorphism between $L\simeq_K L$ and the unit group $(\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^\times$.
-- source:
--   Listed in Mathlib's curated theorem manifests (docs/1000.yaml); formalized in Mathlib as `IsCyclotomicExtension.autEquivPow`. Proof here reduces to that Mathlib result.

